            <ArticleTitle>A case of L-tryptophan-induced eosinophilia-myalgia resulting in death.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>552-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A syndrome of eosinophilia and myalgias associated with the ingestion of L-tryptophan has recently been described. In a large majority of the cases reported to the Centers for Disease Control thus far, discontinuation of L-tryptophan consumption has resulted in complete resolution of symptoms. The author presents a case of L-tryptophan-induced eosinophilia-myalgia syndrome which was progressive despite discontinuation of the L-tryptophan. The condition was refractory to treatment and ultimately resulted in the death of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
